<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boyle Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded 1161</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boyle Abbey is a ruined Cistercian monastery in Boyle, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-roscommon">County Roscommon</a>, Ireland, founded in 1161 as a daughter house of Mellifont. Its church, completed in the early 13th century, combines Romanesque and Gothic features. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macdermot">MacDermots</a> of Moylurg were its patrons; it was suppressed in the 16th century and later used as a military barracks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boyle-abbey.jpg" alt="Boyle Abbey" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas F. Borchert · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boyle_Abbey_Nave_1997_09_17.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
